# Autopilot LM Studio Quality, Routing, And Chat UX Parity Plus Verdict

Verdict: **lm_studio_quality_routing_chat_ux_parity_plus_proven**

## Post-Verdict Erratum - 2026-05-28

A later fresh/default Agent Studio screenshot showed `route.local-first · local:auto` selected and a blocked website artifact response. That invalidated the original wording that product-mode defaults could not surface the fixture/auto placeholder.

Root cause: the Studio selector trusted the active route fallback endpoint before applying the product-model filter, then `studioSnapshotFromState` fell back to the first endpoint/artifact. In an unseeded or stale state that let `endpoint.local.auto` become visible and submit as `local:auto`.

Fix applied after the erratum:

- Product model selection now requires a non-fixture, non-`local:auto` model before the selector can show it.
- If qwen is present in daemon model mounting state, `route.local-first` resolves to `qwen/qwen3.5-9b`, including via `lastSelectedModel`.
- If only fixture/auto records exist, the selector shows `No product model mounted` and submits `__product_model_unavailable__`, which fails closed before artifact generation.
- Stale webview submits carrying `local:auto`, `autopilot:native-fixture`, `stories260k`, or fixture ids are rejected before model invocation.

Support verification after the fix:

- `node --check apps/autopilot/openvscode-extension/ioi-workbench/extension.js`
- `node --check apps/autopilot/openvscode-extension/ioi-workbench/studio/operational-surface.js`
- `node --test apps/autopilot/openvscode-extension/ioi-workbench/extension.static.test.mjs`
- `node --test packages/runtime-daemon/src/conversation-artifacts.test.mjs`
- `npm run test:model-mounting`

Additional selector sanity check against the captured daemon snapshot showed qwen selected when qwen and `local:auto` both exist, and showed `No product model mounted` when only `local:auto` exists.

Autopilot now treats LM Studio as a reference product surface, not as an embedded engine. The qwen/qwen3.5-9b path is Autopilot-native: the daemon mounts and invokes the local GGUF through the cached Vulkan llama.cpp runtime, while the GUI consumes daemon-owned route truth, metrics, artifact lifecycle, and stream events.

## Second Post-Verdict Erratum - 2026-05-28

A second fresh Agent Studio screenshot showed `route.native-local · LM Studio detected` and the same blocked website-artifact response. That invalidated the remaining overclaim that explicit qwen product submissions could not be captured by a non-product endpoint.

Root causes:

- Desktop bootstrap mounted LM Studio-discovered records on `endpoint.electron.model-gui`, so a placeholder `lmstudio:detected` slot could appear as a product route.
- Persisted `backend.llama-cpp` records could keep stale `binary_absent` state even after the launcher discovered the cached Vulkan `llama-server`.
- The daemon selector resolved an explicit model id by the first matching endpoint, so `qwen/qwen3.5-9b` could evaluate an autodiscovered LM Studio endpoint before the native route fallback and then fail policy.

Fix applied after the second erratum:

- Desktop bootstrap now gives the product GUI endpoint only to `provider.llama-cpp` and rejects `lmstudio:detected`, `local:auto`, fixture ids, and external-provider detections for product Studio routes.
- The launcher discovers the cached native llama.cpp server and the local GGUF bytes, then seeds `route.local-first` and `route.native-local` as local-only routes with `provider_eligibility: ["llama_cpp"]`.
- Dynamic backend seeding overwrites stale derived backend fields so a newly discovered llama.cpp binary clears old `binary_absent` state.
- Explicit model routing now prefers the selected route's matching fallback endpoint before any other endpoint with the same model id.

Support verification after the second fix:

- `node --check packages/runtime-daemon/src/model-mounting.mjs`
- `node --check scripts/launch-autopilot-ide-fork.mjs`
- `node --check apps/autopilot/openvscode-extension/ioi-workbench/extension.js`
- `node --test apps/autopilot/openvscode-extension/ioi-workbench/extension.static.test.mjs`
- `node --test scripts/lib/model-mounting-ui-contract.test.mjs`
- `node --test scripts/lib/model-mounting-daemon-contract.test.mjs`
- Fresh desktop boot projected `route.local-first` and `route.native-local` to `endpoint.electron.model-gui` on `provider.llama-cpp`, model `qwen/qwen3.5-9b`, backend `backend.llama-cpp`, with spawned Vulkan `llama-server`.
- Live daemon invocation with `model: "qwen/qwen3.5-9b"` and route `route.local-first` returned content in 2.5s through the native route.
- Live artifact-shaped website completion returned a complete `<!DOCTYPE html>...</html>` document through the native route, fixture-free, with `finish_reason: "stop"`.

