## Product Decisions

- Preserve the Autopilot/OpenVSCode look; add LM Studio-equivalent components only where they fit the workbench.
- Keep model execution semantics daemon-owned. The GUI renders controls and metrics but does not own route truth, invocation semantics, artifact execution, or cleanup.
- Treat LM Studio settings as a breadth reference. Autopilot ports missing primitives into the native model mounting/router contract rather than depending on LM Studio internals.
- Keep raw receipts, route payloads, fixture details, and trace IDs out of product chat; they live in tracing/evidence.

## Remaining Blockers

None for the P0 campaign scope. P1 long-tail provider knobs remain product-decision rows in the manifest, not blockers to this parity-plus verdict.

